{"author":"lars@oddbit.com","body":"This appears to be a firmware issue on the R6400v1 routers -- it looks like the bootloader asserts 192.168.1.1 on the network when it first turns on, and possibly something else asserts the address on a wireless interface before rc_startup runs. This means the only real solution would be to:\n\n- Give gw.house a new address on the 192.168.1.0/24 networks, or\n- Select a new CIDR for the local network.\n\nI am leaning towards 192.168.64.0/23."}